        "abstract": "IT should be obvious by now that to write acceptable editorial material for any publication, you need to have some knowledge of its publishing philosophy and its reader audience. It is not enough to know what audience is reached, but it is essential to know the kind of editorial impact made upon the reader. In any case it would be best to project your article idea in the form of an outline or synopsis (a query) rather than toss a finished manuscript over the transom at the editors. If this isn't done, one may be subjecting his manuscript to a very substantial job of recasting to fit the reader audience.",
